      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ إِنِّي أَقْرَأُ اَلْقُرْآنَ فَتُهْدَى إِلَيَّ اَلْهَدِيَّةُ فَأَقْبَلُهَا قَالَ \"لاَ\" قُلْتُ إِنْ لَمْ أُشَارِطْهُ قَالَ \"أَ رَأَيْتَ إِنْ لَمْ تَقْرَأْهُ أَ كَانَ يُهْدِي لَكَ\" قَالَ قُلْتُ لاَ قَالَ \"فَلاَ تَقْبَلْهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3676 - Al-Hakam ibn Miskin narrated from Qutaybah ibn Al-A'sha who said:\nI said to Abu Abdillah (as), \"I recite the Quran, and gifts are given to me-should I accept them?\"\nImam (as) said: \"No.\"\nI said: \"What if I did not stipulate it (as a condition)?\"\nImam (as) said: \"Tell me, if you had not recited it, would they have given you a gift?\"\nI said: \"No.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Then do not accept it.\""
        ]
      }
    },
